---
title: Data flow - Stuart rotates a key with an SMT Beacon, Satoshi checks each Beacon Signal
---

%% Technical version of the hand sketch "btcr2 data flow visualization".
%% Sketch element → diagram element:
%%   smiley at the left → Stuart; smiley with a top hat at the right → Satoshi
%%   stars and papers → keys, DID document, BTCR2 Signed Update
%%   "Agg" with three small faces and "k/n" → Aggregation Service and Aggregation Cohort: k-of-n signatures
%%     (the specification gives n-of-n as the RECOMMENDED example)
%%   tower → SMT Beacon: the Beacon Address of the cohort, a service in the DID document of Stuart
%%   cloud with a tree → Sparse Merkle Tree (SMT) of the Aggregation Service
%%   "search by did", "Map" → the leaf index of a DID is hash(did); the SMT maps each index to a leaf value
%%   "signed? yes" → k of n participants sign the Beacon Signal; its Signal Bytes are the SMT root
%%   "Sidecar" stack, one row for each dot → Sidecar Data: one entry for each Beacon Signal
%%   "K1" → did:btcr2:k1 identifier
%%   bar with cells and dots → Bitcoin blocks with Beacon Signals
%%   "Q", "inclusion, non-inclusion, gibberish", tall box with 3 parts → the 3 states of the leaf of Stuart
%%   faces under the bar → the leaf state for each Beacon Signal
%%   crossed-out figure → not used
%% Icons are the same as in data-movement.mmd.

flowchart TB
    classDef actor fill:#f4f4f4,stroke:#555555,color:#111111
    classDef chain fill:#fff1dd,stroke:#f7931a,stroke-width:2px,color:#4a2a00
    classDef agg fill:#efe7fb,stroke:#7e57c2,stroke-width:2px,color:#2e1a4f
    classDef sidecar fill:#e3f4e6,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,color:#123d17
    classDef ok fill:#e3f4e6,stroke:#2e7d32,color:#123d17
    classDef none fill:#f4f4f4,stroke:#777777,color:#333333
    classDef bad fill:#fdecea,stroke:#b3261e,color:#7a1d15

    subgraph Stuart["✍ Write path: Stuart (DID controller)"]
      Keys["🔑 Keys<br/>old key → new key"]:::actor
      Doc["📄 DID document<br/>🆔 did:btcr2:k1…<br/>version N"]:::actor
      Update["🧾 BTCR2 Signed Update<br/>patch: new key<br/>version N + 1"]:::actor
    end

    subgraph Cohort["🤝 Aggregation Cohort"]
      Agg["Aggregation Service<br/>collects one leaf value<br/>from each participant"]:::agg
      SMT@{ shape: cloud, label: "🌲 Sparse Merkle Tree (SMT)<br/>search by did: leaf index = hash(did)<br/>map: leaf index → leaf value<br/>SMT root = Signal Bytes" }
      Signers["✍ k of the n participants sign<br/>(n of n in the example of the specification).<br/>Stuart is one of the n.<br/>Each signer first checks its own leaf."]:::agg
    end
    class SMT agg

    Beacon["🏷 SMT Beacon<br/>Beacon Address of the cohort"]:::chain

    Sidecar[("🧳 Sidecar Data (out of band)<br/>one entry for each Beacon Signal:<br/>🧾 BTCR2 Signed Updates, 🌲 SMT Proofs")]:::sidecar

    subgraph Satoshi["🔍 Resolve path: Satoshi (channel peer)"]
      Resolver["Resolver<br/>takes the Beacon Signals in block order"]:::actor
      Check["🌲 SMT Proof with id = SMT root<br/>search by did: walk from the leaf<br/>at hash(did) up to the SMT root"]:::actor
      subgraph Q["Q: the 3 states of the leaf of Stuart"]
        Inclusion["✓ inclusion<br/>leaf = hash(hash(nonce) + updateId)<br/>apply the 🧾 update with hash updateId"]:::ok
        NonInclusion["○ non-inclusion<br/>leaf = hash(hash(nonce))<br/>no update: next Beacon Signal"]:::none
        Gibberish["✗ gibberish<br/>no SMT Proof of Stuart gives the SMT root,<br/>for example a leaf value that Stuart did not submit.<br/>With k-of-n, this can occur if Stuart did not sign.<br/>The DID is invalid<br/>(INVALID_SIGNAL_DATA, MISSING_UPDATE_DATA)"]:::bad
      end
      Trusted["🔑 new key trusted<br/>💬 message verified"]:::ok
    end

    subgraph Chain["⛓ Bitcoin blockchain"]
      direction LR
      B1["block 1<br/>⛓ ⛓<br/>✓ ✓ earlier updates"]:::chain
      B2["block 2<br/>no Beacon Signal"]:::none
      B3["block 3<br/>⛓<br/>✓ inclusion"]:::chain
      B4["block 4<br/>no Beacon Signal"]:::none
      B5["block 5<br/>⛓ key rotation<br/>✓ inclusion"]:::chain
      B6["block 6<br/>⛓<br/>○ non-inclusion"]:::chain
      B7["block 7<br/>no Beacon Signal"]:::none
      B8["block 8 (example)<br/>⛓<br/>✗ gibberish"]:::bad
      B1 --- B2 --- B3 --- B4 --- B5 --- B6 --- B7 --- B8
    end

    %% Stuart makes the update
    Keys -->|"🔑 new key"| Doc
    Doc -->|"📄 patch, 🔖 source and target hashes"| Update
    Keys -->|"✍ proof with the old<br/>capabilityInvocation key"| Update
    Doc -.-|"🏷 service in the DID document"| Beacon

    %% The cohort aggregates and signs
    Update -->|"🔖 leaf value for hash(did)"| Agg
    Agg -->|"builds"| SMT
    SMT -->|"🌲 SMT Proofs,<br/>📝 Unsigned Beacon Signal"| Signers
    Signers -->|"signed? yes: ✍ k signatures"| Beacon
    Beacon -->|"⛓ Beacon Signal<br/>Signal Bytes = SMT root"| Chain

    %% Stuart gives the data to Satoshi
    Update -->|"🧾"| Sidecar
    SMT -->|"🌲 SMT Proof of the leaf of Stuart"| Sidecar
    Sidecar -->|"🧳 with 🆔 did:btcr2:k1…<br/>and 💬 message"| Resolver

    %% Satoshi checks each Beacon Signal
    Chain -->|"⛓ Beacon Signals of the 🏷 Beacon Addresses<br/>in the DID document of Stuart"| Resolver
    Resolver --> Check
    Check --> Inclusion
    Check --> NonInclusion
    Check --> Gibberish
    Inclusion -->|"after the last Beacon Signal"| Trusted
    NonInclusion --> Check
